(ns power
  "KAMI Power — power analysis for digital designs. Restored from the
  legacy kami-engine/kami-power Rust crate (deleted in kotoba-lang/
  kami-engine PR #82 'Remove Rust workspace from kami-engine') as part of
  the clj-wgsl migration (ADR-2607010930, com-junkawasaki/root).

  UPF power intent parsing, static/dynamic power estimation, IR drop grid
  analysis, and electromigration rule checking — one namespace per
  original Rust module:
    power.upf        — Unified Power Format (UPF) text parser + validation
    power.estimation — static (leakage) + dynamic (switching) power formulas
    power.ir-drop     — resistive power-grid IR drop via Gauss-Seidel relaxation
    power.em          — electromigration rule checking

  Zero-dep portable CLJC — pure data + pure functions/parsers, no IO/GPU.
  IR-drop's Gauss-Seidel solve is coarse-grained per-analysis (bounded
  500-iteration relaxation on a small grid), matching ADR-2607010930's
  CLJC scope, not a per-frame hot loop.")
